# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# An alert's button goes DOWN under the hand and answers when the hand
# lets go ON it -- so a press that wanders off before letting go answers
# nothing, which is the one way to change your mind about an alert.
# The alert is the one alert.script raises: dragging the folder onto
# its own sub-folder, which cannot be done and says so with one button.
wait 10
press 200 117
move 200 110
move 200 97
release 200 97
wait 25
expect-alert exists
note the button up: Cancel is the default here, so its face is the
note desk's accent
expect-pixel 646 306 336698
note pressed and held: the alert is still here, the button is down
press 668 301
wait 4
expect-alert exists
note and down: the face darkens under the hand
expect-pixel 646 306 2b5680
note the hand wanders off and lets go there: nothing is answered
move 500 500
wait 4
release 500 500
wait 6
expect-alert exists
note pressed and released ON it: now it answers
click 668 301
wait 8
click-row 2
wait 4
expect-narrate b.txt
quit
